Game Design Document: Card-Based Roguelike
1. Game Design Document (GDD)
1.1 Core Concept (The Guild Builder)
A roguelike "Party-Builder" using a modified standard card set. Unlike traditional card games where cards are spells you cast and forget, here your cards are your Party Members. You are the Leader (Face Card), managing a roster of adventurers, creatures, or specialists. Key Twist: This is a Dual-Rank lane-based game. You deploy your cards onto a persistent board. They stay and fight until they are exhausted or destroyed. Your goal is to manage this "Guild" or "Party" effectively to defeat the Level 7 Superboss.
1.2 The Resources
●	HP: Leader Health. Reaching 0 = Death. Protected by the Vanguard.
●	Deck Count (The Roster): The number of members remaining in your reserve. Reaching 0 = Game Over (Party Disbanded/Wiped).
○	Fatigue Mechanic (Exhaustion): Every time the discard pile is shuffled back into the deck, 1 card is permanently removed from the encounter (Retreats due to injury/exhaustion).
●	Dice (Action Points): Dice are rolled into a "Dice Pool." The sum determines the total value (Mana/Energy) available to deploy units or use skills that turn.
○	Tactical Actions (RNG Mitigation):
■	Action: Exertion: Discard 1 Card (Bench a member) to add half its value to your Dice Pool. Solves "Mana Screw" (Low Dice vs High Cost Cards).
■	Action: Reserve (Passive): Bank up to 2 unspent Dice (their complete value) for the next turn.
1.3 Card Suits & Functions (The Dual-Rank System)
Every card has a Vanguard Effect (Front Row) and a Rearguard Effect (Back Row). The specific visual flavor depends on the Class, but the mechanical identity is constant.
●	♠️ Spades (Strikers / Aggression):
○	Vanguard (Melee): HP = Face Value. Deals damage equal to current HP to the targeted unit. The primary damage dealers.
○	Rearguard (Ranged/Poke): Deals fixed damage (e.g., 2 for low cards, 4 for high). Targeting Logic: Automatically targets the enemy with the Lowest Current HP (to finish off weak foes).
●	♣️ Clubs (Defenders / Wards):
○	Vanguard (Tank): HP = Face Value x 1.5 (rounded up). Deals damage to Vangaurds that struck it (thorns). High HP sponges to soak hits and deal chip.
○	Rearguard (Reinforce): Grants Shield equal to half Face Value to the ally directly in front of it until the shield breaks (occupies slot until shield is gone).
●	♥️ Hearts (Menders / Vitality):
○	Vanguard (Siphon/Paladin): HP = Face Value. Deals damage equal to half Face Value. Lifesteal: Heals itself for half of the damage dealt. Overheal: If at Max HP, excess healing restores the Leader's HP at 1/4 the damage value.
○	Rearguard (Support): Heals the unit directly in front of it for half Face Value.
●	♦️ Diamonds (Class Skills / Sorcery):
○	Function: Instant Actions played directly by the Leader. These are Spells/Abilities, not units. They do not occupy a board slot and are discarded immediately after use (unless otherwise stated).
○	Mechanic: Each specific Rank (2-10) corresponds to a named Spell unique to that Class Deck. The effect is specific to the card, often involving dice rolls or status effects, rather than just scaling off the number.
○	Class-Specific Examples:
■	4♦️ (The Adventurer) - "Get Off Me!": Deal 1d6 damage to a random enemy. Repeat this effect for every friendly Spade unit on the board.
■	7♦️ (The Night Sister) - "Throat Slit": Destroy a target enemy unit if its HP is less than 7. If successful, your Leader gains Stealth (Untargetable) for 1 turn.
■	9♦️ (The War Chief) - "Blood for Blood": All friendly Vanguard units take 4 Damage, but gain +8 Attack for this turn.
■	2♦️ (The Fallen Squire) - "Last Stand": Target Vanguard unit cannot die this turn (HP cannot drop below 1).
■	8♦️ (The Earth Mother) - "Strangleroot": Stun a target enemy. Deal 1 Damage to it for every empty slot on your board (the forest grows into the gaps).
■	5♦️ (The Iron Emperor) - "Overclock": Targeted friendly Club unit attacks immediately, but takes 3 Damage (self-inflicted) after the attack resolves.
■	3♦️ (The Acolyte) - "Submit to the Lord": Deal 2 Damage to all enemy units. Heal all friendly units for 2 HP.
■	10♦️ (The Matriarch) - "Dominate": Seize control of all of your enemy Support units. Move them to your Rearguard. They are added to your deck.
■	6♦️ (The Grand Hierophant) - “Allfather’s Wrath": Deal damage to a target enemy equal to your Leader's Missing HP.
■	5♦️ (The Alchemist) - "Volatile Mixture": Deal 4 Damage to a target. If this kills the target, gain 3 Gold.
■	8♦️ (The Archmage) - "Relativistic Magecraft": Draw 2 cards. Swap their Dice Costs for this turn only.
■	10♦️ (The Merchant Prince) - "Just Business": No Dice Cost, spend 50 Gold. Destroy a target enemy unit instantly (bosses are immune).
1.4 The Player Board & Combat Logic
A. Structure (The 12-Slot Grid) The player commands a formation of 12 slots, creating a deeper tactical field.
●	Row 1 (Vanguard): 5 Slots (V1 - V5).
○	Function: The "Melee" zone. Units here physically block enemies and protect the Rearguard.
○	Capacity: 5 Units.
●	Row 2 (Rearguard): 7 Slots (R1 - R7).
○	Function: The "Support/Reserve" zone. This wider backline allows for extensive support chains, artillery batteries, or protected healers.
○	Capacity: 7 Units.
○	Note: Because the Rearguard is wider than the Vanguard, the outer slots (R1 and R7) are "Flanks." They are harder for melee enemies to reach but may have limited range for certain support buffs that rely on "unit directly in front."
B. Movement & Swapping
●	Permanent Deployment: Once a card is played into a slot, it cannot move to another slot or row manually.
●	Replacement Rule: You may play a card onto an Occupied Slot. The existing unit is Retired (Placed in Discard Pile; "On Death" effects do NOT trigger). The new unit is deployed at full HP.
●	Retreat: You may voluntarily "Retreat" (discard) a unit to free up a slot without playing a new card.
●	Feats: Only specific Class Feats (like the Mercenary's "Command"), Passive Relic Effects, or Diamond Abilities can physically move/swap units after deployment.
C. Combat Phase Resolution (Step-by-Step)
1.	Start of Turn: Trigger "Start of Turn" effects (e.g., Regeneration, Poison).
2.	Deployment Phase: Player spends Dice to play cards or Diamonds.
3.	Player Action Phase:
○	Rearguard Trigger: Backline units act.
■	Support Logic: Heals/Shields apply to the unit directly in front.
■	Ranged Logic: Ranged attacks fire at the enemy with the Lowest HP.
○	Vanguard Strike: Frontline units attack the enemy directly across from them (Melee).
■	Cross-Lane Targeting: If the enemy directly in front is dead/empty, the Vanguard unit attacks the nearest enemy (priority: Left, then Right).
4.	Enemy Response Phase:
○	Enemy Action: Enemies activate from Left to Right.
○	Melee Logic: They attack the Player's Vanguard in their lane.
○	Breach Logic: If a Vanguard slot is empty, the enemy breaks through and attacks the Rearguard slots behind it.
■	Flank Vulnerability: If the entire Vanguard is wiped, enemies prioritize center Rearguard units first unless an ability targets Flanks.
○	Leader Strike: If the defensive line is broken (Relevant Vanguard and Rearguard slots empty), the enemy attacks the Leader (HP) directly.
5.	End of Turn: Cleanup temporary shields, trigger "End of Turn" effects, reduce cooldowns (if any).
D. Persistence & Death
●	Survival: Units on the board retain their current HP between turns.
●	Death: When a unit reaches 0 HP, it is removed and placed in the Discard Pile. It is not Exhausted (permanently lost) unless a specific enemy ability or effect triggers it.
1.5 Enemy Design
Enemies are played as "Hands" of cards lying on the table in a line or grid.
●	The Intent System: Before the player acts, every enemy displays an Intent Icon showing their planned action for the turn.
○	Sword: Attacking (Damage value shown).
○	Shield: Buffing Armor/Block.
○	Sparkles: Casting a Debuff or Special Ability.
○	Skull: Preparing a heavy/fatal attack.
●	The Horde: Enemies, consisting of a variety of vanguards, supports, reserves, etc.
●	The Frontline (Attacker): The card(s) currently engaging the player's Vanguard.
●	The Backline (Supports): Cards behind the Frontline.
●	Rotation Mechanic: When the enemy Frontline dies, the Support immediately behind it or to its left steps forward.
1.6 Class Roster (The Face Cards)
Face cards are not drawn. They sit on the board as the "Leader" avatar. They determine your starting deck, stats, and unique mechanics.
Suit: Spades (The Path of Aggression)
Suit: Spades (The Path of Aggression)
