2. Queen of Spades - "The Night Sister"
●	Lore: Inducted into an ancient order of secret assassins, the Night Sister knows but one purpose: to kill. She cared little for the frantic shouting of the ministers and clerics as she took a long look at the depiction of her target. Finally, her family would spill blood worthy of their blades.
●	Feat: "Flicker Blade" - Once per turn, pay 1/4 the targeted card's Cost (rounded up) to apply a stack of Bleed to it (Deal 2 dmg per turn). Cannot target the same unit twice in a row.
●	Passive: "In Shadows We Lurk" - All friendly Vanguard units have a 5% Dodge Chance. Vanguard Clubs (Tanks) gain double this chance (10%).
3. King of Spades - "The War Chief"
●	Lore: Never has he known a priest whose faith could withstand the edge of his axe, but the loss of his son to the hands of evil itself has set him on a new, treasureless path. Summoning the strongest of the 5 clans to his side, the War Chief sets out to cut down what has robbed him of his only and final joy, come what may.
●	Feat: "Rip and Tear" - Pay 1 HP + the remaining HP of a friendly unit. Sacrifice that unit to deal damage equal to its full Face Value to an enemy.
●	Passive: "Run the Sea Red" - When a friendly unit is below 25% HP (rounded down), it becomes Enraged (can attack twice) but is destroyed at the start of your next turn.
Suit: Clubs (The Path of Protection)
1. Jack of Clubs - "The Fallen Squire"
●	Lore: He failed to save his knight from darkness, leaving him with naught but a half-melted shield and vow of silence. Now he wanders the ruins as the sky spoils itself black, placing himself between monsters and the helpless. But does he do so to recover his honor, or to become a martyr himself? His group of peasant followers believe the former, at the very least.
●	Feat: "Stand Firm" - Pay 2 Dice Points to grant a target unit "Taunt" and +2 HP for one turn.
●	Passive: "Adamant Will" - The first time a Vanguard unit would take fatal damage in an encounter, it gets back up with 1 HP (once per encounter).
2. Queen of Clubs - "The Earth Mother"
●	Lore: She is the lady of the deep woods, where roots strangle stone and bark is harder than steel. The trunks of trees rot from a maligned influence, and she feels each and every ounce of sap dry in their withered branches. She journeys forth not just for the sake of life itself, but silence the endless screams of the forest.
●	Feat: "Overgrowth" - Pay 3 Dice Points. All empty Vanguard slots fill with "Thorny Vines" (0/3 Walls with Thorns 1).
●	Passive: "Rooted" - Friendly units cannot be moved or displaced by enemy abilities. Clubs in the Rearguard grant +1 Regen to the unit in front of them.
3. King of Clubs - "The Iron Emperor"
●	Lore: A king who replaced his failing flesh with clockwork and steel. He believes that flesh is weak and fleeting, but the machine is eternal. His "subjects" are automatons of his own design, marching in perfect, terrifying unison.
●	Feat: "Reconstruction" - Pay X Dice Points to heal a target Mechanical unit (Clubs count as mech) for X * 2.
●	Passive: "Living Metal" - All Club units gain +1 Armor (Reduce all incoming damage by 1, minimum 0).
Suit: Hearts (The Path of Vitality)
1. Jack of Hearts - "The Acolyte"
●	Lore: He found God in the plague-wards, watching the sick die as the medicine men juggled their vials and incense. When the Great Rot began to spread from the north, he saw a vision of its source in the blinding light of the corpse pyres. Realizing that prayer was no longer enough he ventured forth Holy book in one hand, and mace in another, chanting his hymns, as droves of the devoted followed in his path.
●	Feat: "Martyrdom" - Pay 2 HP (Leader) to heal a target Unit by 4.
●	Passive: "Shared Suffering" - Whenever the Leader takes damage, all Vanguard units heal for 1 HP.
2. Queen of Hearts - "The Matriarch"
●	Lore: An ancient Vampire who has seen empires rise and fall. She does not fear the end of the world for she is its Empress, but she nonetheless resents the encroaching void, seeing it as little more than a pest that threatens to consume her cattle. She seeks to drain the source of this rot to purify her feeding grounds to secure her Coven's immortality, then the world may end.
●	Feat: "Blood Tithe" - Destroy a friendly unit. Gain HP equal to its remaining HP.
●	Passive: "Crimson Feast" - All Heart units in the Vanguard gain Hemophilia (Heal self for 50% of damage dealt, rounded down).
3. King of Hearts - "The Grand Hierophant"
●	Lore: The head of the Church of Eternal Light, great-great-grandson to the prophet Alvar himself. He views the spreading shadow not just as an enemy, but as a blasphemy against existence. Carrying his Allfather’s sealed sword, he leads a crusade of templars to the depths of the corruption, convinced that only by purging the source of this darkness, for only he can usher in a promised age of light.
●	Feat: "Divine Intervention" - Pay 4 Dice Points. Revive the last destroyed unit with half HP but 0 Attack into the vanguard slot.
●	Passive: "Overflowing Grace" - Any healing done to a unit already at Max HP is converted into Shields.
Suit: Diamonds (The Path of Sorcery)
1. Jack of Diamonds - "The Alchemist"
●	Lore: Expelled from the Guild for "unintended bodily inversion" and “heretical use of guild materials," this rogue scholar wanders the wastes. They view the apocalypse not as a tragedy, but as a harvest of rare ingredients. They head towards the source of the corruption not to destroy it, but to distill its essence into the ultimate potion, one that will finally show those old fools he is not to be underestimated.
●	Feat: "Transmute" - Pay 3 Dice Points. Destroy a card in your hand (remove from encounter) to create a random Diamond card (Rank 2-4) in its place.
