●	Feat: "Bribe" - Pay 5 Gold (Run Currency). Stun a target enemy unit for 1 turn.
●	Passive: "Deep Pockets" - You start the run with 50 Gold. Shops always offer 1 extra item slot.
1.7 Progression & Meta
A. The Run Structure
●	7 Levels (The Campaign): A run consists of 7 distinct levels. Each level is a map of nodes leading to a specific Level Boss.
●	Pathing: After a victory, players choose their next node from three options:
○	Skirmish: Standard Difficulty. Average rewards.
○	Elite Battle: High Difficulty. Higher chance of better rewards (Rare cards, more gold, small relic chance).
○	Event: Non-combat text encounters that utilize your Dice Pool.
■	Mechanic: The event presents a hurdle (e.g., "A heavy iron gate"). You roll your current Dice Pool and allocate dice to specific solutions based on your Class/Deck.
■	Example (The Locked Crypt):
■	Option A (Force): Smash the Lock. Requires 10+ Total Value. (Reward: Loot).
■	Option B (Finesse): Pick the Lock. Requires a Pair of Dice. (Reward: Loot + Stealth buff).
■	Option C (Sacrifice): Blood Key. Pay 5 HP. (Reward: Cursed Loot).
■	Option D (Class - Alchemist): Melt it. Discard 1 Diamond Card. (Reward: Loot + Upgrade).
●	Rest Sites: Rare nodes where players can Heal the Leader, upgrade a non-diamond cards stats, or exchange a diamond card.
●	Shops: Nodes where players spend Gold earned from battles.
○	Economy Standard: Average Fight = 5 Gold. Elite Fight = 10 Gold. Common Card Cost = 15 Gold. Rare Card Cost = 30 Gold. Joker/Relic Cost = 50+ Gold.
○	Inventory: Buy new Unit cards (Spades/Clubs/Hearts), rare Diamond Spells, or Relics (Passive Buffs).
○	Services: Pay to "Retrain" (Upgrade) a card or "Dismiss" (Remove) a card from the deck to thin out weak units.
B. Recruitment (Building the Guild)
●	Post-Battle Draft: Upon winning a combat node, the player is presented with 5 Cards.
○	Draft Pick: You may select 1 card to add to your deck.
○	Skip: You may skip drafting to gain a small amount of Gold (Run Currency).
●	Rarity Scaling (Value Distribution):
○	Level 1: Common: 2-4. Rare: 5.
○	Level 2: Common: 2-5. Rare: 6.
○	Level 3: Uncommon: 2. Common: 3-6. Rare: 7.
○	Level 4: Uncommon: 2-3. Common: 4-7. Rare: 8.
○	Level 5: Uncommon: 2-3 Common: 4-8. Rare: 9.
○	Level 6: Uncommon: 2-4 Common: 5-9. Rare: 10.
○	Level 7: Uncommon: 2-5 Common: 6-9. Slightly less rare: 10. High chance for Diamond cards.
C. Level Bosses (Levels 1-6)
●	Concept: These are specialized encounters that test specific aspects of your deck. They introduce "Twisted Rules"—global passives that persist for the fight.
●	Examples:
○	The Pyromancer: "Scorched Earth" - Any unit remaining in the same slot for more than 1 turn gains a stack of burn each turn after, applying 1 damage per stack at the start of the turn. Promotes movement/swapping/regen.
○	The Mirror Knight: "Reflection" - All direct damage dealt to the Boss is reflected back to the attacker as half True Damage (pierces shields). Promotes healing/distributed damage dealing/DOT/AOE.
○	The Plaguebearer: "Rot" - Below half health, healing effects are reversed into damage. Promotes shielding/evasion over restoration/high card cycling/diamond usage.
D. The Superboss (Level 7)
●	Concept: The final challenge. These bosses do not just bend rules; they break them. They require a fully optimized Guild/party/band to defeat.
●	Examples:
○	The Grandmaster: "Counterspell" - Negates the first diamond played per turn.
○	The Time-Eater: "Temporal Lock" - Forces the player to end their turn after playing exactly 2 cards, regardless of remaining Dice.
○	The Dealer: "Repo Man" - Steals a card from your hand every turn and plays it against you (discards diamonds, uses one of his own).
○	The Swarmhost: “Tide of Flesh” - When a unit dies a unit with half its vale spawns in the position immediately behind it, or becomes a reserve.
E. The Forge (Meta-Progression)
●	Currency: Renown (Earned at the end of every run, win or lose, depending on progress, difficulty, etc).
●	Upgrades: Renown is spent to permanently upgrade specific Face Cards (Classes).
○	Rank Up (Leader Stats): Increase Starting HP (+2 per rank) or Starting Gold.
○	Logistics (Dice): Unlock the ability to start with extra dice instead of just 2d6, (2d6+1d4, 3d6, 5d4, etc, with costs scaling with power).
○	Training (Feats): Reduce the Dice Cost of the Class Feat or increase its potency, add new effects, exchange the feat for another.
○	Veterancy: Unlock other unique effects that improve your power floor (e.g., Start with a specific Rank 5 Spade instead of a random one, always start with a 7 of diamonds that can be used starting turn 2, round start - fill the middle support slot with a 4 of clubs, etc).
1.8 Jokers (Wildcards)
Jokers are rare, powerful "Guest Cards" that do not adhere to standard deck building rules. There are 4 Joker Archetypes, each corresponding to the "Ultimate Form" of a specific Suit's philosophy.
Universal Rule: Consumable (Guest) All Jokers are Consumable.
●	Units (Spade/Club/Heart): Stay on the board for the duration of the fight (or until destroyed), but are removed from your deck permanently after the battle ends, having fulfilled their contract.
●	Artifacts (Diamond): Are Exhausted immediately upon use and removed from the run.
1. The Slayer (Spade Archetype - Legendary Unit)
●	Concept: A legendary assassin or beast of war.
●	Function: A summonable unit (occupies a slot) that deals massive damage.
●	Example: The Black Knight: Spend any amount of dice points and have that be the attack value (fixed) / 20 HP. Trait: Unrelenting Strikes (Attacks pierce and do true damage [ignore shields]).
2. The Sentinel (Club Archetype - Legendary Unit)
●	Concept: An immovable object or magical construct.
●	Function: A summonable unit (occupies a slot) that fills a non-dps often tank role.
●	Example: The Iron Colossus: 0 Attack / 50 HP. Trait: "Guardian" - Cannot attack. Takes damage for ALL friendly units (Taunt All Lanes). Immune to Status Effects.
3. The Saint (Heart Archetype - Legendary Unit)
●	Concept: Angelic servant or a mythical healer.
●	Function: A summonable unit (occupies a slot) that grants powerful utilities.
●	Example: The Phoenix: 5 Attack / 5 HP. Trait: "Miracle" - When played, fully heals the Leader and revives one random destroyed unit. Rebirth: When destroyed, returns to your hand instead of the discard pile (once per encounter).
4. The Artifact (Diamond Archetype - Legendary Item/Spell)
●	Concept: Ancient relics, wacky spells, or forbidden scrolls.
●	Function: Instant Actions (played from hand, do not occupy a slot) that create chaotic, game-warping effects.
●	Example: "The Golden Gun": Deal 99 Damage to ANY random target.
●	Example: "The Time Warp": Take an extra turn immediately after this one, lose the turn after that.
●	Example: "Pandora's Box": Replace every card in your hand with a RANDOM COST Diamond card from any unlocked diamond cards from any class, Exhausts the cards that were replaced.
●	Example: "Unlimited Power": Your dice total is now 100, you lose the ability to roll dice at the beginning of the turn (other dice effects still apply), when your dice value reaches 0, you deck out.
1.9 Glossary of Keywords & Mechanics
To ensure clarity during gameplay, the following keywords define specific mechanics.
●	Armor (X): Flat damage reduction. All incoming damage is reduced by X (Minimum 0).
●	Bleed (X): The target takes X damage whenever they attack or activate an ability.
●	Burn (X): The target takes X damage at the start of their turn. The value of X decreases by 1 each turn.
●	Exhaust: Removed from the current encounter. Returned to the deck at the end of the battle.
●	Poison (X): The target takes X damage at the end of their turn. The value does NOT decrease automatically; it must be cleansed.
●	Stun: The target cannot attack or use abilities for their next turn.
●	Taunt: Enemies MUST target this unit if able. If multiple units have Taunt, the enemy chooses the closest one.
●	Stealth: This unit cannot be targeted by single-target attacks. Area of Effect (AOE) damage still hits.
●	Thorns (X): Any unit that attacks this unit with a melee strike takes X damage.
●	Shield: Temporary HP that absorbs damage before HP. Shields are removed at the start of the unit's next turn unless specified otherwise (e.g., "Plated").
●	True Damage: Damage that ignores Shields and Armor, dealing direct HP damage.
●	Silence: Target unit loses all Passive abilities and cannot be triggered by Support effects for 1 turn.
1.10 Relics (Passive Artifacts)
Relics are powerful, passive items found in Shops, Elite Chests, or Events. They provide global buffs to the Leader's party.
●	Common Relics:
○	Weighted Dice: Once per encounter, you may reroll any one die.
○	Officer's Badge: Start every combat with +2 Gold.
○	Whetstone: All Spade units gain +1 Attack.
●	Rare Relics:
○	Vampiric Chalice: Whenever an Elite enemy dies, the Leader heals 2 HP.
○	Pocket Watch: Draw 1 extra card on Turn 1 of every combat.
○	Commander's Helm: Increases your maximum hand size by 1.
●	Boss Relics (Found after beating a Level Boss):
○	Mana Battery: Start every turn with +1 to your Dice Pool total.
○	Necronomicon: All "Exhausted" cards have a 50% chance to return to your deck after the battle instead of being lost.
○	Heavy Crown: Gain +1 Dice every other turn, but enemies start with +1 Strength per turn.
1.11 Core Gameplay Polish (The Fun Factor)
To ensure the game feels fluid and strategic rather than frustratingly random, these core mechanics act as "Safety Valves."
A. Leader Actions (Always Available) Even with a terrible hand or low dice rolls, the Leader can always perform basic actions. These are located on the UI near the Dice Pool.
●	Punch (1 Die): Deal 1 Damage to the nearest enemy.
●	Guard (1 Die): Grant 1 Shield to the Leader (Self).
●	Cycle (2 Dice): Discard 1 card from your hand to Draw 1 card.
B. Battle Fatigue (Anti-Stall) To prevent infinite healing loops, the environment becomes hostile over time.
●	Mechanic: Starting on Round 15, "The Darkness Closes In."
●	Effect: All units (Friendly and Enemy) take 1 True Damage at the end of every turn. This damage increases by +1 every subsequent turn (1, 2, 3, 4...).
C. The "Mulligan"
●	Start of Combat: You may shuffle any number of cards from your starting hand back into your deck and redraw that many. You may do this once per combat.
